# This repository is PUBLIC. Nothing below may ever be committed.
# Reasoning: README.md "What is deliberately not here".

# Proprietary Logitech firmware and config binaries. Share checksums, not files.
*.bin
*.hfw
*.EZHex
*.EZUp
*.EzHex
*.EzUpgrade

# Remote dumps and concordance output. The *-info.txt files carry serial GUIDs.
*-info.txt
*-safe.bin
samples/*
!samples/README.md

# Ghidra projects contain an imported copy of proprietary firmware.
*.gpr
*.rep/
*.lock
ghidra-project/
ghidra_projects/

# Ghidra project built by bin/setup-ghidra.sh, and scratch output.
.ghidra/
work/
# Throwaway analysis scripts. They have to sit inside the workspace to import the packages, so
# they cannot live in a system temp directory, and one session committed a directory of them by
# reflex with `git add -A`.
.scratch/

# Per-machine Claude Code settings. These accumulate absolute paths from whoever's machine
# they were written on. The shared hook configuration lives in .claude/settings.json, which
# is committed.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Third party binaries and anything extracted from one. Proprietary by definition, so they live
# in the lab and only derived facts are published. Deliberately broad: it is cheaper to ignore an
# extension nobody here produces than to discover a gap after a commit.
*.jar
*.dylib
*.jnilib
*.so

# Build and tool noise.
*.class
*.pyc
__pycache__/
.DS_Store

# Node. pnpm-lock.yaml is committed on purpose: direct dependencies are pinned exactly in
# package.json, and the lock file pins the transitive tree the same way.
node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# IDE project state. WebStorm's workspace.xml carries local paths and a per-install GUID, which
# is also why the pre-commit hook noticed it before this line existed.
.idea/
.vscode/
